{"type":"text","timestamp":1788466295906,"sessionID":"ses_f9720c618ffecGLNPbSpSS2lBN","part":{"id":"prt_068e5aa14001uJs7JDAESFD5ke","messageID":"msg_068e519dd001ZlSIHRdzxksKGy","sessionID":"ses_f9720c618ffecGLNPbSpSS2lBN","type":"text","text":"Done. Implemented `at_most` selection in `AgentSet.select` (mesa/agent.py:121), matching the upstream Mesa PR #2253 exactly:\n\n- **`at_most` parameter**: int → fixed upper limit of agents; float (0.0–1.0) → fraction of total agents, rounded down (e.g., `at_most=0.2` on 10 agents → 2)\n- **Backward compat**: `n` still works and emits `DeprecationWarning: The parameter 'n' is deprecated. Use 'at_most' instead.` while converting `n` → `at_most`\n- **Upper-limit semantics**: combined with `filter_func`/`agent_type`, results may be fewer than the max; agents are always returned in AgentSet order (shuffle first for random samples)\n- **Chainable**: works with `sort`, `set`, `shuffle`, e.g. `model.agents.shuffle_do().select(at_most=0.4)` or `agentset.select(at_most=5).set(\"attr\", val)`; `inplace=True` modifies in place, otherwise returns a new AgentSet; omitting `at_most` returns all matches\n\nVerified: full suite `208 passed`, ruff check/format clean, plus scenario checks for both int/fraction selection, filtering combos, in-place mode, and the deprecation warning. Also added the fraction-selection assertions to tests/test_agent.py:62-66.","time":{"start":1788466276884,"end":1788466295900}}}
